{
  "Title": "ELSA-2026-500637: Unbreakable Enterprise kernel security update (IMPORTANT)",
  "Description": "[5.4.17-2136.361.4.4]\n- net: skbuff: propagate shared-frag marker in skb_zerocopy() (Zizhen Liu)  [Orabug: 40326056]  {CVE-2026-99284}\n\n[5.4.17-2136.361.4.3]\n- xen-netback: Fix XenBus connection failure cleanup (Tu Dinh)  [Orabug: 40281452]  {CVE-2026-99286}\n- xen-blkback: Avoid UAF when reading I/O statistics (Juergen Gross)  [Orabug: 40281452]  {CVE-2026-100082}\n- xen-netback: defer xenvif_mcast_addr_list_free() (Jan Beulich)  [Orabug: 40281452]  {CVE-2026-100081}\n- xen-netback: Fix UAF when reading statistics data (Juergen Gross)  [Orabug: 40281452]  {CVE-2026-100080}\n\n[5.4.17-2136.361.4.2]\n- net: restore refcount ordering for lockless socket access (Hyunwoo Kim)  [Orabug: 40285708]\n- inet: reject unhashed sockets during established lookups (Hyunwoo Kim)  [Orabug: 40285708]  {CVE-2026-99288}\n- rcu: Add a hlist_nulls_unhashed_lockless() function (Paul E. McKenney)  [Orabug: 40285708]\n\n[5.4.17-2136.361.4.1]\n- iommu/amd: Force device table to maximum size (Suravee Suthikulpanit)  [Orabug: 40172712]  {CVE-2024-21963}\n- x86/microcode/AMD: Increase PATCH_MAX_SIZE for Family 1Ah (Saeed Mirzamohammadi)  [Orabug: 40172712]\n\n[5.4.17-2136.361.4]\n- vhost-scsi: zero misaligned I/O bounce pages (Shubham Antil) [Orabug: 40193932]\n\n[5.4.17-2136.361.3]\n- KVM: x86: Use active memslots for the per-vCPU MMIO cache (Jinu Kim) [Orabug: 40180571,40201707] {CVE-2026-99082}\n- drbd: fix 'LOGIC BUG' in drbd_al_begin_io_nonblock() (Lars Ellenberg) [Orabug: 39130967] {CVE-2026-23356}\n- rds: cong: fix race while clearing rs_cong_mask (Anand Khoje) [Orabug: 39519861]\n- hugetlbfs: hold trunc_rwsem during hugepage migration (Stephen Brennan) [Orabug: 39541934]\n- ipv4: validate checksum_start before completing checksum (Michael S. Tsirkin) [Orabug: 40165812,40167666] {CVE-2026-99999}\n- netfilter: nfnetlink_queue: unbreak SCTP traffic (Antonio Ojea) [Orabug: 40165812]\n- net: add inline function skb_csum_is_sctp (Xin Long) [Orabug: 40165812]\n- ipv4: free inet_opt and ireq_opt after an RCU grace period (Eric Dumazet) [Orabug: 40165790,40167664] {CVE-2026-98432}\n- vhost: reset the vring metadata cache on vring reconfiguration (Jun Yang) [Orabug: 39917526] {CVE-2026-74580}\n\n[5.4.17-2136.361.2]\n- ionic: serialize hardware timestamp Tx queue access (Joseph Dobosenski) [Orabug: 40061822]\n\n[5.4.17-2136.361.1]\n- net/mlx5: Set parent device before health polling (Manjunath Patil) [Orabug: 39208695]\n\n[5.4.17-2136.360.3]\n- IB/mlx4: delete allocated id_map_entry while sending REJ (Praveen Kumar Kannoju) [Orabug: 39999072]\n- net: tun: bound receive headroom (Asim Viladi Oglu Manizada) [Orabug: 40020673,40036871] {CVE-2026-81000}\n- xfrm: ah6: validate routing header segments_left (Asim Viladi Oglu Manizada) [Orabug: 39982188,40036875] {CVE-2026-80844}\n- inet: frags: strip GSO state from fragments before reassembly (Xinyang Ge) [Orabug: 39972532] {CVE-2026-80590}\n- sctp: prevent peer transport count overflow (Asim Viladi Oglu Manizada) [Orabug: 39886843,40036878] {CVE-2026-74469}\n- pppoe: reload header pointer after dev_hard_header() (Asim Viladi Oglu Manizada) [Orabug: 39859408,40036877] {CVE-2026-68121}\n\n[5.4.17-2136.360.2]\n- Revert 'net/mlx5: Add poll-eq API to be used by ULP's' (Praveen Kumar Kannoju) [Orabug: 39764468]",
